  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed additional storey, by virtue of its height, bulk, and massing when viewed from the rear elevations of Nos. 7 to 17 (odd) Crown Lane, would be an overbearing and dominant form of development resulting in an unacceptable loss of outlook, perceived by those neighbouring properties including the enjoyment of their amenity space. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the policies of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024 and is refused in accordance with paragraph AB.2.(1)(g) of Class AB of Part 20 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The proposal by reason of its inadequate natural light to serve the flats which would be north facing with no rear windows would represent a substandard and inappropriate form of accommodation which would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. The proposal is thereby contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan, Policy CP4 of the Enfield Plan Core Strategy, Policies DMD8 of the Development Management Document, the Technical Housing Standards-Nationally Described Space Standards and the guidance contained within the National Planning Policy Framework and  Article 3(9A) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of a comprehensive legal agreement securing the development as 'car-free', would contribute unacceptably to parking congestion in the Southgate Circus Town Controlled Parking Zone which would give rise to conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of vehicular traffic and pedestrians, and fail to promote the use of non-sustainable modes of transport, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (2024) and thereby fails to satisfy Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AB, Paragraph AB.2. Condition (1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (Amendment) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The proposed flank windows to Flat 8 as indicated on drawing No. D01 Rev. F would fail to accord with the requirements of Class AB, Paragraph AB.2. Condition (3) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (Amendment) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), which requires that any development under Class AB is only permitted subject to the condition that the development must not include a window in any wall or roof slope forming a side elevation of the building. The proposed flank windows would therefore require planning permission."
  ],
